page DocsSourceControl

title "Source control - Documentation"

template
<div class="min-h-[calc(100vh-4rem)] grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] bg-page transition-colors">

  <DocsSidebar active="source-control" />

  <div class="min-w-0 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-10 py-6 sm:py-10">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

    <article class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel p-5 sm:p-8">
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Documentation / Source control</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-light uppercase tracking-wide text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Source control</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-sm mt-2 mb-8">Source control is where your code lives. Connect your GitHub or GitLab account here, and your sites can deploy from your repositories. Open the page with Source control in the sidebar.</p>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border-l-2 border-l-brand-500 bg-brand-500/5 px-4 py-3 mb-8">
        <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">Connect your account before you create a site from a repository. A site with a repository can then deploy new code with one button: see <a href="/docs/sites/create" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Creating a site</a> and <a href="/docs/sites/deployment" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Deployment</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Connecting an account</h2>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">The connect button is at the top right of the page. You choose GitHub or GitLab, give the connection a label, and enter your username and the access token you made at GitHub or GitLab.</p>

      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 mb-8">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span>Create the token in your GitHub or GitLab settings first, and give it access to the repositories you want to deploy.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span>You can connect more than one account, for example a personal one and one for your company.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span>The label is only for you. Pick something that tells the accounts apart.</span></li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">The list</h2>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Each connected account is a card:</p>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-4">

        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">GitHub or GitLab</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">At the top left of the card: which service the account is on.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Status</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">At the top right of the card. It shows the state of the connection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Label and username</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The name you chose, and the account's username written with an @ in front.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold mb-3">Buttons on each card</h3>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">

        <div class="px-5 py-4">
          <h4 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-semibold">Edit</h4>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">Opens the same form you used to connect the account. Use it to rename the connection, or to paste a new token when the old one has expired or been revoked.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="px-5 py-4 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <h4 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-semibold">Remove</h4>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">Asks you to confirm: select Yes, remove, or Cancel to back out. It disconnects the account from Tylix Deploy. Your repositories at GitHub or GitLab are not touched.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border-l-2 border-l-brand-500 bg-brand-500/5 px-4 py-3 mb-8">
        <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">Before you have connected anything, the page shows "No accounts connected": "Connect GitHub or GitLab to create sites from your repositories."</p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">If something goes wrong</h2>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden">

        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't remove that connection.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">A red message above the list. The account is still connected. Try again.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">A deploy cannot pull the code</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The usual cause is a token that has expired or lost access to the repository. Create a new token, use Edit on the account to paste it, then deploy again.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-8 pt-5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
        <a href="/docs/registrars/billing" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">&larr; Domain billing</a>
        <a href="/docs/settings/members" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Members &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
  </div>
</div>